Teach the desktop install classifier about package-managed installs.

FLUXDOWN_INSTALL_SOURCE is upstream's own env var for "this came from a
container or NAS package" (detect.rs:16), and classify_server already maps it to
UpdateManualReason::ManagedPackage. classify_desktop ignores it, so a desktop
build installed by a package manager still classifies as LinuxPortable and the
in-place updater tries to replace the executable. In the Nix store that write
cannot succeed: linux_package_owner() only inspects /opt/fluxdown via dpkg/pacman,
and APPIMAGE is unset.

This honours the existing variable on the desktop path too. No new enum variant:
ManagedPackage already exists. `kind` stays LinuxPortable and asset_keys stays
populated, so update checks still tell the user a new version is out — only the
self-replacement is withheld, which is correct for a read-only store.

--- a/native/agent/src/update/install/detect.rs
+++ b/native/agent/src/update/install/detect.rs
@@ -138,6 +138,12 @@
     };
     let manual_reason = if !facts.official_build {
         Some(UpdateManualReason::UnofficialBuild)
+    } else if facts
+        .install_source
+        .as_deref()
+        .is_some_and(|source| !source.trim().is_empty())
+    {
+        Some(UpdateManualReason::ManagedPackage)
     } else if matches!(
         kind,
         UpdateInstallKind::Docker
